Three color-coded clusters in left-to-right flow, grouped by what the engineer sees: (1) PyCS Infrastructure --- frozen framework consumed as-is (bisos.csSeed .spcs mechanism, bisos.fileObj walker + branch .spcs framework + WalkExampleSpec); (2) Custom Seed --- the one thing authored per new domain (a domain-seed CSXU with walkExamples() plus its leaf .spcs); (3) Planted Tree --- the on-disk BPO tree the engineer builds by planting, not by writing Python. Today's concrete instance is bisos.dockerProc + bro_dockerfiles; future instances (lcntProc, staticWebProc, ...) follow the same pattern.
